# The cold-chapter case, RIGHT half: it does the pressing. Two presses.
#
# The first lands inside the harness's low-heap window and crosses a section boundary, which is what
# a chapter build looks like from the reader's side. Both halves cross on it, because a paired turn
# advances the spread, and both should put their link down for the build.
#
# The second lands after the window has passed and the link is back. It is the check that the
# suspension cost the pair nothing durable: the spread still advances by two, with no re-negotiation
# in between.
log pageflip-heapbuild-right: start
expect_timeout 90000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
expect peer present
# Inside the low-heap window, and across a chapter boundary.
wait 13000
tap down
# Well after the window closes and the link is back.
wait 9000
tap down
wait 8000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-hb-right-00.bmp
wait 1500
log pageflip-heapbuild-right: done
quit
